Explanation: 
\@2:Z scale: - This is the Z-axis (vertical/height) scale parameter for data channel 2
V [Sens. TM Deflection] - The measurement is in Volts, specifically the Tapping Mode (TM) cantilever deflection sensor signal
(0.0003750000 V/LSB) - The conversion factor: each Least Significant Bit (LSB) of the raw 16-bit integer data equals 0.000375 Volts. So to convert raw data counts to actual voltage, you multiply by this factor
0.01852148 V - The full-scale range or maximum voltage value that can be measured with this setting

